{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c42b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0af73-29fd-7160-afe2-ea4709b071c8"},"sequence":112,"recorded_at":1780531400000219,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c700f538-d9a2-4b6d-a603-1bdd1bb0d054","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"c700f538-d9a2-4b6d-a603-1bdd1bb0d054","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c700f538-d9a2-4b6d-a603-1bdd1bb0d054"},"call_id":"call_01a0af7354ec70b780714021f4adea11","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2x16gz/TASK-260830-2x16gz_ordering-decision.md`.\n1|# Peer authentication prerequisite ordering\n2|\n3|Primary execution decision, 2026-09-08. This repairs implementation-board order under the existing full-project goal; it does not introduce a product rule or remove a conformance case.\n4|\n5|## Evidence\n6|\n7|TASK-260830-2x16gz requires seven hostile-peer/failure cases. Its accepted prerequisites are signed checkpoints43c0e2b9 (peeridentity) andc1eff016 (sshtransport), with independently accepted treesc775903a andf1dbf8f2. They deliberately do not claim runtime bilateral host admission. Pinned AX section11.1 requires both sides to verify protocol host_id after external SSH authentication; section11.2 defines the actual hello envelope. Existing TASK-260830-z1yxg9 owns that implementation but was blocked by2x16gz. Its other prerequisites treeox and33sfxc are both done. The producer's blocked-outcome and recovery evidence establish this ordering cycle without changing product files.\n8|\n9|## Supported repair\n10|\n11|Move the entire existing TASK-260830-z1yxg9 from STORY-260830-4qojoz into STORY-260830-1kiyj6. Its normative scope and acceptance criteria remain the same: envelope/hello, correlation, maps, namespace/cardinality, limits, deadlines and structured errors. Its code/rule ownership remains attached to the same task; no second handshake owner or substitute authorizer is created.\n12|\n13|Replace its dependency on2x16gz with the accepted SSH transport task1tvg8e, preserving its other prerequisites. Make2x16gz depend onz1yxg9 as well as1tvg8e. Keep2x16gz as the final peer-auth conformance leaf, with all seven cases open. Add2x16gz as a prerequisite of the subsequent negotiation task219okr so another Story cannot start from an undelivered foundation. Remaining negotiation/closed-operation tasks stay in4qojoz.\n14|\n15|The enlarged peer-auth Story will therefore deliver identity -> SSH transport -> actual RPC envelope/hello admission -> hostile-peer conformance in one managed worktree and one final Story delivery. No accepted checkpoint needs to be rewritten merely to accommodate a missing final CR. The original RPC Story retains negotiation and closed-operation conformance using the delivered prerequisite.\n16|\n17|## Bounds and gates\n18|\n19|Only apply after the stopped conformance recovery chain releases its workspace normally; preserve every accepted commit and any uncommitted work. Use task-board mutations, including its journaled set_parent, never board-file edits. Verify resulting graph has no dependency cycle, the new producer is ready, and conformance is still blocked on its actual prerequisite. All role spawns remain Codex Astra high/medium with fresh preflight.\n20|\n21|The seven-case test description remains intact. Native changed-key and SSH ciphertext-replay evidence still require real hermetic external-SSH fixtures; config parsing or exit255 simulation is insufficient. Disclosure proof must be tied to the exact section6.4 policy enforcement and any actual runtime consumer needed for the claimed consequence; no network-publisher proof may be inferred from a policy string. If further implementation prerequisites are demonstrated, route those while preserving the requirement; do not mark a named row N/A simply to land.\n22|\n23|Qualified-selector product syntax for TASK-260830-21gygk is a separate unanswered user decision. This ordering repair does not answer it. Source CI debt remains pending and never counts as passed.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c42d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0af73-29fd-7160-afe2-ea4709b071c8"},"sequence":113,"recorded_at":1780531400000221,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c700f538-d9a2-4b6d-a603-1bdd1bb0d054","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"c700f538-d9a2-4b6d-a603-1bdd1bb0d054","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c700f538-d9a2-4b6d-a603-1bdd1bb0d054"},"call_id":"call_01a0af7357907648a8c0098742bb1804","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2x16gz/TASK-260830-2x16gz_producer.md`.\n1|Own TASK-260830-2x16gz (test-peer-auth-and-hostile-network-failures), the FINAL leaf of STORY-260830-1kiyj6 (peer-configuration-and-authentication). Predecessors on the Story branch, all accepted and checkpointed: 2u34k1 (host/peer identity), 1tvg8e (SSH transport and command boundary), 2ez769 (internal/hosttrust credentials, enrollment, rotation/revocation, authorization generations, Config-4 migration; ResolvedPaths pair), z1yxg9 (internal/rpcwire RPC 5.0.0 and internal/hostchannel Host Channel 1.0.0 with the HC-* fixture families; its verdict left two P3 notes you must close: an \"ax-host/2\" same-family ALPN refusal vector in TestVerifyPeerRefusals, and a shortened-deadline hook for the ~10 s TestInvalidActivation/bad_destination vector). You are the primary implementation-conformance owner for the pinned v0.6.0 Section 11.10.4 / AC-HOST-001 product gate (\"Drive the real Config-4 launch and RPC-5 dispatch on supported SSH/platform lanes: full mutual TLS, exact enrolled certificate/UUID/hello, no preauthentication effects, migration/downgrade refusals, fresh-key rotation, revocation of idle/live streams within one second, expiry and concurrent mutation-generation fencing; exercise valid and invalid actual certificates, both role failures, stale/failed reads and recovery bypasses; model fixtures alone never satisfy this gate\"), retaining the task's historical scope (unknown peers, key changes, spoofed host IDs, disconnects, replay, oversized frames, disclosure mismatches fail closed; Sections 6, 11.1, 16.1). Deliver an executable conformance suite over the landed production entries (hostchannel.Dial/Serve/Call, hosttrust enrollment/rotation/revocation/generation, config Config-4 selection, the SSH transport boundary of 1tvg8e) — no new product model: (1) real carrier lane — run the responder as a real child process behind a real OpenSSH loopback carrier where the host allows it (/usr/sbin/sshd is present: start an unprivileged sshd on 127.0.0.1 with a temp host key, a temp authorized_keys and a forced/exact command executing the AX responder over the ordered stdio stream; skip with an explicit, asserted reason if sshd cannot bind in this environment) and prove Section 11.10.1 end to end: TLS records are the first bytes on the stream, no PTY, no banner, stderr bounded; native Tailscale SSH is a stated bound (HC-PARITY by construction; record it as not executed, never as passed); (2) hostile-network matrix through the real channel — unknown peer (unenrolled root), key change (re-issued leaf under an enrolled root is not enrolled), spoofed host ID (valid cert for UUID A presenting hello ID B, and a cert whose SAN names B), destination mismatch, disconnect at every phase boundary (before TLS, mid-handshake, after handshake before hello, after hello, mid-request, mid-response — each yields transport_failure or the specified class with no partial effect and no durable write), replay (a recorded TLS flight and a recorded encrypted hello replayed on a fresh connection must be refused by TLS 1.3 itself — assert the failure class, and the nonce correlation rule for a replayed hello inside one session), oversized frames (8 MiB line, 5 MiB object, 1 MiB handshake cap versus Go's 256 KiB record cap — document which fires), disclosure mismatch (a peer presenting different identity facts in hello and certificate; contracts.rpc other than [\"5.0.0\"]; Structured Error version drift), timeout/race (silent peer past the handshake and hello deadlines; a peer stalling mid-request against the configured RPC timeout; two concurrent connections from one peer), custody (leaf private key read from a wrong-permission file or a foreign store refused by the ResolvedPaths pair; a copied key authenticates until revoked — assert both halves as the pinned text states), revocation and generation (revoke a live peer: idle and in-flight streams close within one second per the pinned text — measure it; rotation admits the new tuple only after explicit enrollment, retire_at bounds, no second rotation before revocation; a stale generation at dispatch and at a mutation boundary refused under concurrent mutation), migration/downgrade refusals (Config-4 selecting a legacy route, an RPC-4 hello on the host channel, a plaintext preface), both role failures (initiator refuses a bad server; responder refuses a bad client), stale/failed reads (an unreadable trust store or marker is an integrity failure, not \"absent\"), recovery bypasses (a retry that changes the operation ID or body is refused; no new-session/fresh-handle substitution); (3) every vector asserts the exact Section 15 class and exit and that nothing durable changed (census the state dir before/after); (4) the Section 11.10.5 upstream policy vectors are source evidence only — do not implement a policy reader and do not claim their synthetic passes as executed support; (5) narrowing mutants for every new assertion family with a shipped harness (per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, an applied harmless SURVIVED control), plus the seven original conformance cases of this task re-derived with n-of-m through the authenticated channel; (6) a conformance matrix mapping every AC-HOST-001 clause, HC-* gate and hostile-network row to a test, a not-executed stated bound (native Tailscale SSH; platform lanes other than this host) or NOT APPLICABLE with owner. This is the FINAL leaf (story_final CR): carry the Story-close items — internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json bindings for 6.6/11.10/11.10.1-11.10.5/16.1 and the acceptance case AC-HOST-001 bound to the real conformance suite with honest coverage text (executed lanes versus stated bounds), reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 re-pinned (precedent Stories 3drr2m/3jqsx1/3m2mw8/2jylym); README sections for internal/hostchannel/rpcwire (if missing) and your suite with test commands and no capability claim (no ax command exists); LOGBOOK entry; the candidate's task-board.config.json must remain byte-identical to trunk except the rpcwire fuzz gate already added by z1yxg9 (if you add a conformance command, say so explicitly and keep it bounded). Managed Story worktree contract: .temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-1kiyj6 whose tip is the z1yxg9 checkpoint; the preserved packet directories under .temp are read-only; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; origin/main has moved to e4e3e88 (release-agnostic validation command 21) — run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2x16gz first and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>; before handoff verify git status shows only candidate paths (no __pycache__, no .pyc; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1). Evidence contract as in the repository DoD. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured validation suite once before the handoff; hand off no later than 3.5 hours in (an 8-point leaf: if the full matrix cannot be finished, hand off a reviewable slice with the remaining rows enumerated precisely — the Story-close items are mandatory). Attach TASK-260830-2x16gz_results.md, TASK-260830-2x16gz_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-2x16gz_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260830-2x16gz --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be muse-spark xhigh while codex is out of quota.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
