{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d355","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0af73-29fd-7160-afe2-ea4709b071c8"},"sequence":2053,"recorded_at":1780531400004101,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c700f538-d9a2-4b6d-a603-1bdd1bb0d054","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"c700f538-d9a2-4b6d-a603-1bdd1bb0d054","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c700f538-d9a2-4b6d-a603-1bdd1bb0d054"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0af82-6a45-7652-a7e6-e11751caf5d5"},"task_id":"01a0af82-6a45-7652-a7e6-e11751caf5d5","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0af82-6a45-7652-a7e6-e11751caf5d5","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-74-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cat > /tmp/rev3/merge_logbook.py <<'EOF'\\nours = open(\\\"/tmp/rev3/merge3/LOGBOOK.md.ours\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\").read().splitlines(keepends=True)\\ntheirs = open(\\\"/tmp/rev3/merge3/LOGBOOK.md.theirs\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\").read().splitlines(keepends=True)\\n# leaf entry block: ours lines 8..16 (0-based 7..16): ### + 7 bullets + blank\\nassert ours[7].startswith(\\\"### TASK-260830-2x16gz\\\"), ours[7][:60]\\nassert ours[15] == \\\"\\\\n\\\", repr(ours[15])\\nassert ours[16] == \\\"## 2026-09-17\\\\n\\\", ours[16]\\nblock = ours[7:16]\\nassert sum(1 for l in block if l.startswith(\\\"- \\\")) == 7, len(block)\\n# theirs head shape\\nassert theirs[5] == \\\"## 2026-09-17\\\\n\\\", theirs[5]\\nassert theirs[6] == \\\"\\\\n\\\", repr(theirs[6])\\nassert theirs[7].startswith(\\\"### TASK-260830-2atgj4\\\"), theirs[7][:50]\\nmerged = theirs[:7] + block + theirs[7:]\\nopen(\\\"/tmp/rev3/merge3/LOGBOOK.final.md\\\", \\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\", newline=\\\"\\\").write(\\\"\\\".join(merged))\\nprint(\\\"logbook merged: theirs=%d ours-block=%d final=%d\\\" % (len(theirs), len(block), len(merged)))\\nEOF\\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 /tmp/rev3/merge_logbook.py\\ncp /tmp/rev3/merge3/LOGBOOK.final.md LOGBOOK.md\\nhead -n 20 LOGBOOK.md\\necho \\\"===diff HEAD --stat for the 6===\\\"\\ngit diff HEAD --stat -- LOGBOOK.md README.md internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json internal/traceability/traceability.go internal/traceability/traceability_test.go internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go\",\n  \"description\": \"Merge LOGBOOK and install\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"logbook merged: theirs=2372 ours-block=9 final=2381\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n- F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\n- F2 (MEASURED BOUND): an idle stream with zero traffic does NOT self-close within one second of revocation — `serveLoop` carries no background watchdog. The next dispatch fences in milliseconds and `WatchGeneration` reports the commit; recorded as a stated bound with log evidence, not a pass. Tailscale SSH and non-host lanes likewise bounded.\\n- F3: `os/exec.Cmd.Wait` called twice hangs the second caller forever — test cleanup consumes one `Wait` channel. The 8 MiB line cap is enforced twice (framing + decode), so the oversize mutant weakens both layers in one multi-file probe (harness extended for `(file, old, new)` triples). The Structured Error schema URN is `urn:ax:schema:error`; a drift vector with the wrong URN passed for the wrong reason until the mutant survived and exposed it.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 9 new narrowing probes, all killed by named `TestHostile*` vectors (same-family ALPN, dual-layer oversize, client rebind, rpc-contracts, error-version drift, truncated-dispatch ignore, snapshot integrity, correlation, static nonce); pre-existing 26 probes re-run green (neutral passed, client-cache documented SURVIVED). Per-plant logs/tables in the outcome tar.\\n- TRACEABILITY: `AC-HOST-001` registered over 20 suite tests; new `unevidenced` bindings for 11.10.1–11.10.4 + 16.1 with honest gaps (executed lanes vs stated bounds); 6.6/11.10 gaps refreshed; 11.10.5 stays unowned by design (no policy reader); digest re-pinned `e327bb08...`; report 102 cases / 61 bindings / 8 unowned / 17/487 clauses; README figures + tracecheck pins updated.\\n- AC: 7 of 7 hostile rows + 13 of 13 executed AC-HOST-001 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in the outcome evidence). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed. NOTE: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate` replay against `origin/main e4e3e88` fails on a LOGBOOK.md rebase conflict (missing replay resolution) — orchestrator-side integration issue, worktree untouched at `244a7dc`.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2atgj4 — property-test the ownership reducer (final leaf)\\n\\n- SCOPE: executable proofs of the four story-pinned ownership invariants\\n  (union-order independence, loser preservation, clock non-authority,\\n===diff HEAD --stat for the 6===\\n LOGBOOK.md                                        |   9 +\\n README.md                                         |  25 ++-\\n internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go |   8 +-\\n internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json       | 195 +++++++++++++++++++---\\n internal/traceability/traceability.go             |   2 +-\\n internal/traceability/traceability_test.go        |  10 +-\\n 6 files changed, 211 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4053,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1014,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
