{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d70f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0af73-29fd-7160-afe2-ea4709b071c8"},"sequence":2530,"recorded_at":1780531400005055,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c700f538-d9a2-4b6d-a603-1bdd1bb0d054","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"c700f538-d9a2-4b6d-a603-1bdd1bb0d054","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c700f538-d9a2-4b6d-a603-1bdd1bb0d054"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0af94-52b8-7840-ad27-37b768b6097a"},"task_id":"01a0af94-52b8-7840-ad27-37b768b6097a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0af94-52b8-7840-ad27-37b768b6097a","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev3/results-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2x16gz results rev2 — base refresh + reconcile + full revalidation\n2|\n3|Role: developer (republish run, no re-implementation).\n4|Rev1 outcomes (`TASK-260830-2x16gz_results.md`, `..._conformance-matrix.md`,\n5|`..._producer-evidence.tar.gz`) remain the implementation evidence; this rev2\n6|record covers the base refresh, the candidate reconcile, and the rerun of the\n7|full configured suite on the new base. All implementation ratios and bounds\n8|from rev1 stand unchanged.\n9|\n10|## 1. Refresh record\n11|\n12|Story branch `task-board/story/STORY-260830-1kiyj6`, worktree\n13|`.temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree`.\n14|\n15|- Pre-refresh tip: `244a7dce2f687c58238b1b11fbba67d618521632` (z1yxg9 checkpoint).\n16|- Old trunk base: `62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e`.\n17|- Fresh authority: `origin/main = e4e3e8834675cf3814effd3b2673b4931dfbf311`\n18|  (STORY-260917-158jyi release-agnostic catalog gate + board-state record).\n19|- Command: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2x16gz`\n20|  (+ `--replay-resolutions /tmp/republish-2x16gz/resolutions.json`).\n21|- Outcome: `refresh_advanced`, new tip\n22|  `c3de159762f3e3d0a926ece0b0d4231abb669562`.\n23|\n24|Replayed checkpoints (original -> replayed, all `git verify-commit` Good for\n25|`oparin@me.com`, parent chain reaches `e4e3e88`):\n26|\n27|| # | Original | Replayed | Subject |\n28||---|---|---|---|\n29|| 1 | `efe119a` | `14d1176bc794e460db6cf48d7436d3ccb601baa1` | 2u34k1 host/peer identity |\n30|| 2 | `5e54874` | `4677a87bc4588c5e4d412a775113d4d51727f8a7` | 1tvg8e SSH transport |\n31|| 3 | `ae5a4cc` | `a14f718288902627340f5f8086e9c984e060191a` | 2ez769 credentials/config4 |\n32|| 4 | `244a7dc` | `c3de159762f3e3d0a926ece0b0d4231abb669562` | z1yxg9 RPC envelope/hello |\n33|\n34|Checkpoints 1–2 replayed without conflict. Checkpoints 3–4 each stopped once\n35|on a `LOGBOOK.md` append-append conflict; each was resolved with a\n36|checkpoint-bound replacement (template\n37|`{\"version\":1,\"branch_oid\",\"trunk_oid\",\"candidate_tree_oid\",\"resolutions\":[...]}`):\n38|\n39|| Resolution | `checkpoint_oid` (REBASE_HEAD) | Replacement sha256 | Bytes |\n40||---|---|---|---|\n41|| 1 | `ae5a4cc5394ef80fc2fc3ef12965acc0670cb5a4` | `53ae8caf766ab8e929ec36c36e1457fb5789d71a2621a54ea92ba9618bc2208e` | 464104 |\n42|| 2 | `244a7dce2f687c58238b1b11fbba67d618521632` | `ef8d5804d4e7581e4a0a455aeef7f64e5eef42ead97cba3060608c80b6dbb077` | 467766 |\n43|\n44|Resolution rule (both): trunk's newer entries first, then the replayed\n45|checkpoint's added block(s), everything else byte-identical. Verified per\n46|resolution: `diff` against the replay side is a pure insertion (zero\n47|deletions), every `### ` entry from both sides present, zero duplicates, zero\n48|conflict markers. Note: the ae5a4cc checkpoint adds LOGBOOK entries in two\n49|places (top rev12..09-10 block plus an end-of-file `## 2026-09-10 (later)`\n50|CR3/rev8/rev9 block); both were carried.\n51|\n52|Replay-fidelity verification (all four checkpoints):\n53|\n54|- `git diff <original> <replayed> --name-only` equals exactly the 28-file\n55|  trunk delta `62d4463..e4e3e88` (comm both directions empty).\n56|- Every trunk-delta file except two is byte-identical between the replayed\n57|  tree and `e4e3e88`. The two exceptions are correct 3-way unions, verified\n58|  both directions: `README.md` (story Host-Trust section + trunk `-adopted`\n59|  docs) and `task-board.config.json` (story rpcwire fuzz gate + trunk\n60|  `-adopted` command 22).\n61|- `git diff 244a7dc c3de159 -- internal/hostchannel internal/traceability`\n62|  is empty (replay preserved the story implementation byte-for-byte).\n63|\n64|## 2. Stale-copy audit (carried candidate vs new HEAD)\n65|\n66|Pre-refresh safety: full candidate diff + both new test files copied to\n67|`/tmp/republish-2x16gz/` before the refresh; the worktree-local `.task-board`\n68|checkout artifact (spuriously modified by an earlier session running board\n69|commands inside the worktree) was restored to `HEAD` before the refresh so\n70|the carried delta held only the 13 candidate paths.\n71|\n72|Trunk delta (`62d4463..e4e3e88`) is 28 files: 22 `.task-board` records,\n73|4 `internal/catalog` files, `LOGBOOK.md`, `README.md`, `task-board.config.json`.\n74|\n75|| Carried path in `git status` | In trunk delta? | Disposition |\n76||---|---|---|\n77|| 8 `.task-board/...` paths (new-trunk records missing from stale copy) | yes | `git checkout HEAD -- .task-board` (artifact, not candidate) |\n78|| `internal/catalog/catalog.go`, `catalog_test.go`, `cmd/cataloggen/main.go`, `cmd/cataloggen/main_test.go` | yes | `git checkout HEAD -- <each>` (stale pre-refresh copies; this task never touched catalog) |\n79|| `task-board.config.json` | yes | `git checkout HEAD -- task-board.config.json`; verified `cmp` equals `HEAD` exactly (`HEAD` = trunk `-adopted` command 22 + story rpcwire fuzz gate, both intentional) |\n80|| `LOGBOOK.md` | yes | Hand merge: candidate 2x16gz entry kept newest-first on top, then `HEAD` content byte-identical. `git diff HEAD` = 11 insertions, 0 deletions |\n81|| `README.md` | yes | Hand merge: restored trunk's two `-adopted` regions (regenerate block, Go-toolchain row) verbatim; kept candidate figure rewrites (101->102 / 56->61 / 12->8) and hostile-suite docs. `git diff HEAD` = 22 insertions + 3 figure-line rewrites only |\n82|| `internal/hostchannel/*` (5 tracked + 2 new), `internal/traceability/*` (4) | no | Untouched carries; tracked diff byte-identical to pre-refresh backup (modulo diff index lines); new files sha256-identical to backup |\n83|\n84|Digest pin: `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` stays\n85|`e327bb08ae514279a8ab2b1f0ec58d02a5d368ca593cc14f3c3dd5f5dc6b14ba`.\n86|No re-pin was required: trunk did not touch the traceability registry or its\n87|pins, the carried registry is byte-identical to the reviewed rev1 bytes, and\n88|`tracecheck` exits 0 with the pinned digest (report: 102 cases / 61 bindings /\n89|8 unowned, matching the README figures).\n90|\n91|Final `git status`: exactly the 13 candidate paths (11 modified + 2 new),\n92|no `__pycache__`, no `.pyc` (`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` throughout).\n93|Candidate left UNCOMMITTED on the story branch; no commit, no push, no board\n94|edit from this run beyond status/evidence.\n95|\n96|## 3. Full validation rerun on `c3de159` (all observed this run)\n97|\n98|Configured suite = 27 commands from `task-board.config.json`\n99|(`spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands`):\n100|\n101|| # | Command | Result |\n102||---|---|---|\n103|| 1 | `gofmt` clean check | pass |\n104|| 2 | `go build ./...` | pass |\n105|| 3 | `go vet ./...` | pass |\n106|| 4 | `go test ./... -count=1` | exit 0, 31 packages ok, 0 FAIL |\n107|| 5 | `go test ./... -race -count=1` | exit 0, 31 ok, 0 FAIL, 0 data races |\n108|| 6 | `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | exit 0 (config 92.9, hostchannel 84.1, hosttrust 76.3, localstore 83.7, peeridentity 97.5, rpcwire 97.8, secprim 94.4 — identical to rev1) |\n109|| 7–20 | 14 fuzz smokes (rpcwire 1, scalar 1, canonicaljson 4, secconftest 8) | 14/14 pass |\n110|| 21 | `tracecheck` | exit 0; 102 cases / 61 bindings / 8 unowned / 17/487 clauses |\n111|| 22 | `cataloggen -adopted ... -check` (new trunk form) | exit 0, no generated drift |\n112|| 23–24 | `GOOS=linux/windows go build ./...` | exit 0 both |\n113|| 25 | JSON parse over tracked `*.json` | pass |\n114|| 26 | `task-board validate` | exit 0; 191 pre-existing board-hygiene issues, 0 referencing this task |\n115|| 27 | `git diff --check` | clean |\n116|\n117|Own suites (this run):\n118|\n119|- `go test ./internal/hostchannel -run 'TestHostile' -count=1 -v`: exit 0,\n120|  54 `--- PASS`, 0 FAIL. `TestHostileRealCarrierOpenSSH` PASS (0.25 s —\n121|  OpenSSH loopback lane executed, not skipped). The single SKIP is\n122|  `TestHostileSSHHelperResponder`, the helper-process guard (skips unless\n123|  invoked as the forced-command child — by design).\n124|- Mutation batteries were NOT rerun in this republish run: reconciliation\n125|  changed zero bytes of production or test source (hostchannel/rpcwire diff\n126|  `244a7dc..c3de159` is empty; carried candidate bytes identical to backup),\n127|  so the rev1 battery evidence (9/9 new probes killed, 26 prior probes\n128|  re-run) still binds to this exact source. Full behavioral suites above\n129|  were rerun instead.\n130|\n131|## 4. Coverage restatement (unchanged from rev1)\n132|\n133|- Hostile rows: 7 of 7 driven (`Dial`/`Serve`/`Call`).\n134|- AC-HOST-001 rows: 14 of 15 fully driven; B8 partial (measured bound).\n135|- HC-* families: 10 of 10. P3 notes: 2 of 2 closed.\n136|- Stated bounds unchanged (native Tailscale SSH, non-host lanes, idle\n137|  self-close measured, 11.10.5 policy reader by design, no `ax` CLI).\n138|- No unsupported capability advertised; README/hostchannel docs and the\n139|  traceability bindings already updated in the carried candidate.\n140|\n141|## 5. Handoff evidence (rev2)\n142|\n143|- `TASK-260830-2x16gz_results-rev2.md` (this file)\n144|- `TASK-260830-2x16gz_conformance-matrix-rev2.md` (rev1 matrix + refresh addendum)\n145|- `TASK-260830-2x16gz_producer-evidence-rev2.tar.gz` (real gzip: rev2 suite/\n146|  r