ce evidence only | No policy reader implemented (by design); unowned registry entry retained with fresh gap |\n103|| No `ax` CLI / SSH process launch in product | `LaunchArgv`/`LaunchForConfig` compute argv only; carrier test's forced command execs `Serve` via the test binary; `SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND` proves the exact `ServeArgv` words crossed the wire |\n104|| `LaunchForConfig` nil-binding branch unreachable via public entries | Config loader requires closed `mesh.host_channel` in v4; branch is defense-in-depth behind the loader gate (no mutant — unreachable, documented) |\n105|| TLS alert text, handshake-failure races on `Dial` side | Owned by crypto/tls + rendezvous timing; class pinned (`transport_failure`), message not pinned |\n106|\n107|## E. Narrowing-mutant summary — 9 of 9 new probes killed\n108|\n109|Harness: `internal/hostchannel/mutations.py` (extended with multi-file\n110|`(file, old, new)` plants for the dual-enforced line cap). Full behavioral\n111|suite per plant; sources untouched (overlay). Pre-existing 26 probes re-run:\n112|neutral passed, 24 killed, 1 documented harmless SURVIVED (`client-cache`).\n113|\n114|| Mutant | Narrowing (admits exactly) | Named killing test | Result |\n115||---|---|---|---|\n116|| `alpn-same-family` | `ax-host/2` ALPN | `TestVerifyPeerRefusals/alpn-same-family` | killed |\n117|| `oversize-dispatch` | 8 MiB+10 line at framing AND decode | `TestHostileOversizedFrames/dispatch_line_8mib_plus_one` | killed |\n118|| `stale-client-rebind` | one generation past the client binding | `TestHostileRecoveryBypass/stale_binding_never_rebinds` | killed |\n119|| `rpc-contracts` | any `contracts.rpc` disclosure | `TestHostileDisclosureMismatch/responder_contracts_drift` | killed |\n120|| `error-version-drift` | a 1.2.0 error honored as 1.3.0 | `TestHostileDisclosureMismatch/error_version_drift` | killed |\n121|| `truncated-dispatch-ignored` | one truncated dispatch frame skipped instead of unframeable close | `TestHostileDisconnectPhases/mid_request_close` | killed |\n122|| `snapshot-integrity` | corrupt store read as empty store | `TestHostileStaleReadsAreIntegrityFailures/corrupt_store` | killed |\n123|| `correlation-health` | miscorrelated `health.get` answer accepted | `TestHostileRecoveryBypass/response_id_mismatch_refused` | killed |\n124|| `nonce-static` | one constant hello nonce | `TestHostileReplayNonceFreshness` | killed |\n125|\n126|Gates without a new mutant name their covering probe: supplement exact-match\n127|(`match-leaf/match-root/match-spki/match-count`), trust-state\n128|(`state-revoked/state-retiring`), hello identity (`hello-id-server/client`),\n129|resumption (`tickets`), limiter (`handshake-cap`), CA bound (`ca-bound`),\n130|server generation (`stale-dispatch`), mutation rebind (`stale-mutation`).\n131|Replay refusal is TLS-1.3-intrinsic (stdlib owns the gate; ours are\n132|no-tickets/no-cache/fresh-nonce, all mutated). No new source-text-inspecting\n133|gate was added (the static census + its token-preserving evasion mutant are\n134|prior work, re-run green).\n135|\n136|## F. P3 notes from z1yxg9 — 2 of 2 closed\n137|\n138|| Note | Resolution |\n139||---|---|\n140|| Same-family `ax-host/2` ALPN refusal vector in `TestVerifyPeerRefusals` | Added `alpn-same-family` row + `alpn-same-family` mutant, killed |\n141|| Shortened-deadline hook for `TestInvalidActivation/bad_destination` | Explicit 500 ms overrides + < 2 s elapsed assertion |","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
